{% extends "mapper.j2" %}

{% block project_guidance -%}
You are working on the tests for `mngr forward` (`libs/mngr_forward/`), the
proxy that serves each agent at its own `agent-<hex>.localhost` origin behind
a one-time-code session. Its behaviors are observable at the HTTP and
WebSocket surface, so witness them in process wherever that surface reaches:

- Default to `starlette.testclient.TestClient` against the FastAPI app, the
  idiom `imbue/mngr_forward/server_test.py` already uses. Where a path needs
  real network I/O, that file stands up a backend on loopback (real HTTP and
  real `ws_serve` WebSocket servers) rather than reaching outside the test
  process; follow that.
- New witnesses live under `libs/mngr_forward/imbue/mngr_forward/witnesses/`,
  in the module named under "Where tests go"; the existing witnesses in
  `server_test.py`, `auth_test.py`, and `cookie_test.py` are adopted where
  they are.
- Read `libs/mngr_forward/conftest.py` and `imbue/mngr_forward/testing.py`
  before writing new setup, and reuse what is there. Never use unittest.mock
  or monkeypatch.setattr.
{%- endblock %}

{% block infra_blockers -%}
These witnesses run against the proxy's own ASGI app and, where a real socket
is unavoidable, against listeners the test starts on loopback. They need no
cloud credentials, no external services, and no remote host. If a unit
appears to require one, that is a signal you are reaching past the observable
surface: reread the unit and find the claim you can make at the app boundary
before recording a blocker.
{%- endblock %}
